. Eksp. Teor. Fiz. 12, 447 (1970)"}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/63463"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRev.108.1063"],"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"108","artid":"1063","year":1957,"page_start":"1063","journal_title":"Phys.Rev."},"authors":[{"full_name":"Regge, T."},{"full_name":"Wheeler, J.A."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"T. Regge, J.A. Wheeler, Phys. Rev. 108, 1063 (1957). https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.108.1063"}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2454"}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1710.07669","authors":[{"full_name":"Ganguly, A."},{"full_name":"Gannouji, R."},{"full_name":"Gonzalez-Espinoza, M."},{"full_name":"Pizarro-Moya, C."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"A. Ganguly, R. Gannouji, M. Gonzalez-Espinoza, C. Pizarro-Moya, arXiv:1710.07669 [gr-qc]"}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1631958"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRevLett.24.737"],"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"24","artid":"737","year":1970,"page_start":"737","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett."},"authors":[{"full_name":"Zerilli, F.J."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"F.J. Zerilli, Phys. Rev. Lett. 24, 737 (1970), DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevLett.24.737"}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/61120"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRevD.1.2870"],"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"1","artid":"2870","year":1970,"page_start":"2870","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Vishveshwara, C.V."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"C.V. Vishveshwara, Phys. Rev. D 1, 2870 (1970), DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevD.1.2870"}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/61639"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1088/0264-9381/31/16/165016"],"arxiv_eprint":"1311.4543","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"31","artid":"165016","year":2014,"journal_title":"Class.Quant.Grav."},"authors":[{"full_name":"Gannouji, R."},{"full_name":"Dadhich, N."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"R. Gannouji, N. Dadhich, Class. Quant. Grav. 31, 165016 (2014). https://doi.org/10.1088/0264-9381/31/16/165016 . arXiv:1311.4543 [gr-qc]"}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1265060"}}],"number_of_pages":5,"legacy_creation_date":"2012-09-24","preprint_date":"2012-09","author_count":1,"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"5 pages, 1 figure"}],"earliest_date":"2012-09","refereed":true,"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"SPIRES","value":"SPIRES-9785396"}],"facet_author_name":["1046981_Radouane Gannouji"],"core":true,"license":[{"imposing":"arXiv","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"},{"license":"CC-BY-4.0"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1187773","updated":"2023-03-06T17:01:33.952245"},"journal_title_variants":["Eur. Phys. J. C","Eur.Phys.J.C"],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["gr-qc"],"value":"1209.5128"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["A.Nicolis.1","T.Regge.1","M.Gonzalez.Espinoza.1","A.Ganguly.1","C.V.Vishveshwara.1","Sheng.Wang.2","D.S.Gorbunov.1","G.Gabadadze.1","M.Porrati.1","V.I.Zakharov.1","F.J.Zerilli.1","R.Maartens.1","Morgan.May.1","C.PizarroMoya.1","R.Gannouji.1","G.R.Dvali.1","P.Papadopoulos.1","E.Trincherini.1","Kazuya.Koyama.1","E.Papantonopoulos.1","S.M.Sibiryakov.1","K.I.Maeda.1","Zoltan.Haiman.1","N.Dadhich.1","Lam.Hui.1","V.Zamarias.1","Wen.Juan.Fang.1","Wayne.Hu.1","J.Polchinski.1","V.Rezania.1","R.Rattazzi.1","M.Sasaki.1","Hendrik.van.Dam.1","G.Kofinas.1","M.J.G.Veltman.1","J.A.Wheeler.1","T.Shiromizu.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"Nbranch.png","caption":"Existence of the black hole for the DGP branch: The blue part represents the range of the parameters $(\\bar{m},\\bar{q})$ for which the black hole has 2 horizons. In the grey region, the metric is always negative and the white region corresponds to a black hole with only a cosmological horizon, because of the negativity of the effective mass, hence inside the cosmological horizon the solution would be a naked singularity.","source":"arxiv","key":"ae9f0a5ef3c3735cd0b624fc19692e35","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/ae9f0a5ef3c3735cd0b624fc19692e35"}],"legacy_version":"20181121095109.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"},{"term":"Theory-HEP"}],"first_author":{"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"GRID","value":"grid.8170.e"}],"full_name":"Gannouji, Radouane","last_name":"Gannouji","first_name":"Radouane","recid":1046981},"control_number":1187773,"dois":[{"value":"10.1140/epjc/s10052-018-5809-x"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Gannouji:2012wk"],"abstracts":[{"source":"Springer","value":"We find an exact solution on the brane for a static black hole in the DGP model. In the appropriate limit we recover the two known solutions, the Schwarzschild and the Reissner–Nordström solutions with tidal charge. The solution has two branches, which correspond asymptotically to a de Sitter or flat Universe. Finally, we study the linear stability of the solutions. We find that the Regge–Wheeler and the Zerilli potential are positive and conclude on the stability.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Springer"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"We find an exact solution on the brane for static black hole in the DGP model. In the appropriate limit we recover the 2 known solutions, the Schwarzschild and the Reissner-Nordstrom solutions with tidal charge. The solution has 2 branches, which correspond asymptotically to de-Sitter or flat Universe. Also we study the linear stability of the solutions. We find that the Regge-Wheeler and the Zerilli potential are positive. Finally the dipole perturbation is derived which corresponds to a linearization of a rotating black hole solution on the brane.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"title":"DGP black holes on the brane"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"DGP black holes on the brane"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2018-04-20"}],"curated":true}},{"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/632218?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/632218?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/632218?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/632218?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/632218?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/632218?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A632218"},"created":"2003-11-04T00:00:00+00:00","id":"632218","updated":"2023-03-10T14:54:20.371660+00:00","metadata":{"citation_count":256,"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"21","page_end":"404","year":2004,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214779"},"page_start":"391","journal_title":"Class.Quant.Grav."}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":214,"authors":[{"full_name_unicode_normalized":"lobo, francisco s.n.","full_name":"Lobo, Francisco S.N.","curated_relation":true,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1024546"},"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/905609"},"value":"Lisbon U."}],"last_name":"Lobo","ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"Francisco.S.N.Lobo.1"}],"signature_block":"LABf","uuid":"283b3692-b7e8-4857-be60-1a27a44512b0","first_name":"Francisco S.N.","recid":1024546},{"full_name_unicode_normalized":"crawford, paulo","full_name":"Crawford, Paulo","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1012829"},"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/905609"},"value":"Lisbon U."}],"last_name":"Crawford","ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"P.Crawford.1"}],"signature_block":"CRAFADp","uuid":"8847df1d-9c60-4b27-8dcf-3f5e4b9a2d04","first_name":"Paulo","recid":1012829}],"citeable":true,"$schema":"https://inspirehep.